  "fields": {
    "responsibility": "Complete rooted startup/physical initialization/member acceptance, entry+root drain, owner cleanup and unknown native isolation as one whole managed C-target lifecycle replacement.",
    "retired": "Remove resize-only VM owner header/state and allocator-side VM list publication; native launch no longer borrows PSTATE before accepted RUN. Eliminate mutable shared-status branch decisions, in-GC arbitrary destructor calls and ignored global cleanup refusal.",
    "validation": "Complete fixed-cache bootstrap twice phase1-4;408 original GSI; full remaining original Make; all startup failure/marker-GC/multishot/W<R/unknown-survivor/cross-VM cases; actual host cleanup/nested marker refusal; implementation72-action PBT, replay and6-to1 shrink. Existing four QNT modules and five mutation controls; no duplicated Lean.",
    "benefits": "Independent resource/descriptor/root lifetimes: unknown native identity cannot block healthy VM collection, cannot recycle a slot and cannot grant global free. Complete immutable branch/join delivery prevents a slow participant skipping a cut. Gambit precise safe points/shared multi-shot continuations are strengthened, not narrowed to one-shot/private heaps.",
    "costs": "Measured bounded VM control and activation layout in matrix. Entry/member registry CAS, activation allocation, owner queue latency and quarantined native payload remain real costs. No throughput/pause/RSS or whole-SMP completion claim.",
    "process": "Third whole integration candidate owns all22 obligations including current predecessor root/collector requirements. Admission grants3/4 only after five gates and whole delivery; independent SMP stays1/12. Scheduler/request/FIFO/product and full CFFI remain next boundaries.",
    "checklist": "dev/refactoring/modern-c/vm-lifecycle.org#vm-lifecycle-global-reclaim",
    "models": "Native SysML selects22 source/native/programme requirements; actual ASCENT gates reject each missing need. Existing QNT owns schedules incl immutable cut delivery and generation-local abort receipts; Lean conditional algebra unchanged/not rerun. C adapters and actual native consumers establish distinct premises.",
    "open": "Whole request-service/FIFO/scheduler/Gerbil product qualification and hosted CI remain separate. No arbitrary native death, private unregistered reentry/alias, longjmp or indefinite blocking destructor recovery. Foreign payload size is unbounded; explicit generic CFFI release semantics unchanged. Retain old bootstrap and RC/model failures."
  },
